"An application of proof mining to the proximal point algorithm in CAT(0) spaces (https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.09169)\nciteturn3academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.2 years ago; Title: An application of proof mining to the proximal point algorithm in CAT(0) spaces\nTitle: An application of proof mining to the proximal point algorithm in CAT(0) spaces\nAuthors: Laurentiu Leustean, Andrei Sipos\nDate: Fri Jul 28 09:54:19 2017\n\nWe compute, using techniques originally introduced by Kohlenbach, the first author and Nicolae, uniform rates of metastability for the proximal point algorithm in the context of CAT(0) spaces (as first considered by Bacak), specifically for the case where the ambient space is totally bounded. This result is part of the program of proof mining, which aims to apply methods of mathematical logic with the purpose of extracting quantitative information out of ordinary mathematical proofs, which may not be necessarily constructive.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFixed point property for a CAT(0) space which admits a proper cocompact group action (https://arxiv.org/abs/1102.0729)\nciteturn3academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 15.7 years ago; Title: Fixed point property for a CAT(0) space which admits a proper cocompact group actionAuthors: Tetsu Toyoda\nTitle: Fixed point property for a CAT(0) space which admits a proper cocompact group action\nAuthors: Tetsu Toyoda\nDate: Thu Feb  3 16:46:54 2011\n\nWe prove that if a geodesically complete $\\mathrm{CAT}(0)$ space $X$ admits a proper cocompact isometric action of a group, then the Izeki-Nayatani invariant of $X$ is less than $1$. Let $G$ be a finite connected graph, $\\mu_1 (G)$ be the linear spectral gap of $G$, and $\\lambda_1 (G,X)$ be the nonlinear spectral gap of $G$ with respect to such a $\\mathrm{CAT}(0)$ space $X$. Then, the result implies that the ratio $\\lambda_1 (G,X) / \\mu_1 (G)$ is bounded from below by a positive constant which is independent of the graph $G$. It follows that any isometric action of a random group of the graph model on such $X$ has a global fixed point. In particular, any isometric action of a random group of the graph model on a Bruhat-Tits building associated to a semi-simple algebraic group has a global fixed point.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nContemporary Mathematics (https://publish.illinois.edu/ymb/files/2020/04/Sturm-2003-Probability-measures-on-metric-spaces-of-nonpositi.pdf)\nciteturn3search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Probability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive ... Karl-Theodor Sturm ... 3. ... curvature, NPC space, Hadamard space, Alexandrov space, quadruple inequality, variance in-\nContemporary Mathematics\nProbability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive\nCurvature\nKarl-Theodor Sturm\nAbstract. We present an introduction to metric spaces of nonpositive curva-\nture (”NPC spaces”) and a discussion of barycenters of probability measures\non such spaces. In our introduction to NPC spaces, we will concentrate on\nanalytic and stochastic aspects of nonpositive curvature. Among others, we\npresent two diﬀerent characterizations of nonpositive curvature in terms of\nvariance inequalities for probabilities on metric spaces as well as a character-\nization in terms of a weighted quadruple inequality.\nThe latter generalizes\nReshetnyak’s quadruple inequality which played a major role in many devel-\nopments during the last decade. For Riemannian manifolds, nonpositive cur-\nvature will also be characterized by the existence of a contracting barycenter\nmap on the space of probability measures on the respective manifold.\nIn our discussion of barycenters of probability measures on NPC spaces,\nbasic results like the Law of Large Numbers, Jensen’s inequality and the L1-\ncontraction property will be derived and many examples will be presented. We\nidentify barycenters for images, products, L2-spaces, Hilbert spaces, trees and\nmanifolds. Also some results on convex means will be included.\nContents\n1. Geodesic Spaces\n2. Global NPC Spaces\n3. Examples of Global NPC Spaces\n4. Barycenters\n5. Identiﬁcation of Barycenters\n6. Jensen’s Inequality and L1 Contraction Property\n7. Convex Means\n8. Local NPC Spaces\nReferences\n1991 Mathematics Subject Classiﬁcation. Primary 60B, 58E, 28C; Secondary 58C, 52A, 49C.\nKey words and phrases. Barycenter, mean value, expectation, center of mass, nonpositive\ncurvature, NPC space, Hadamard space, Alexandrov space, quadruple inequality, variance in-\nequality, Jensen inequality.\nThe author gratefully acknowledges support by the SFB 611 at the University of Bonn.\nc\n⃝0000 (copyright holder)\n1--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProbability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive Curvature - Karl-Theodor Sturm - Google Books (https://books.google.com/books/about/Probability_Measures_on_Metric_Spaces_of.html?id=za_XHAAACAAJ)\nciteturn3search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # Probability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive CurvatureImage: Front Cover Karl-Theodor Sturm SFB 611, 2003 - 34 pages\n\n# Probability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive Curvature\n\nImage: Front CoverKarl-Theodor SturmSFB 611, 2003 - 34 pages\n\n### Bibliographic information\n\nTitle  | Probability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive Curvature\nIssue 79 of Preprint, Sonderforschungsbereich Singuläre Phänomene und Skalierung in Mathematischen Modellen\nAuthor  | Karl-Theodor Sturm\nPublisher  | SFB 611, 2003\nLength  | 34 pages\nExport Citation  | BiBTeX EndNote RefMan--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProbability measures on metric spaces of nonpositive curvature | CiNii Research (https://cir.nii.ac.jp/crid/1361418518709620864)\nciteturn3search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; # Probability measures on metric spaces of nonpositive curvature ...   * Karl-Theodor Sturm ...     2003\n\n# Probability measures on metric spaces of nonpositive curvature\n\nDOI 被引用文献14件\n\n  * Karl-Theodor Sturm\n    \n    \n\n## 書誌事項\n\n公開日\n    2003\n\nDOI\n    \n\n  * 10.1090/conm/338/06080\n\n公開者\n    American Mathematical Society\n\n## この論文をさがす\n\n  * CiNii Books\n\n## 収録刊行物\n\n  * Contemporary Mathematics\n    \n\nContemporary Mathematics 357-390, 2003\n\nAmerican Mathematical Society\n\n## 被引用文献 (14)*注記\n\n読み込み中...\n\nもっと見る\n\n## 詳細情報 詳細情報について\n\n  * CRID\n    1361418518709620864\n  * DOI\n    10.1090/conm/338/06080\n  * ISSN\n    10983627\n    02714132\n  * データソース種別\n\n## 書き出し\n\n  * RefWorksに書き出し\n\n  * EndNoteに書き出し\n\n  * Mendeleyに書き出し\n\n  * RDFで書き出し\n\n  * Refer/BibIXで表示\n\n  * RISで表示\n\n  * BibTeXで表示\n\n  * TSVで表示\n\n  * CSVで表示--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProbability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive Curvature | Request PDF (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/251422452_Probability_Measures_on_Metric_Spaces_of_Nonpositive_Curvature)\nciteturn3search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 23.8 years ago; Crawled: last month; # Probability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive Curvature  * January 2003 ... Image: Request Full-text Paper PDF ... For Riemannian manifolds, nonpositive cur- vature will also be characterized by the existence of a contracting barycenter map on the space of probability measures on the respective manifold.\nArticle\n\n# Probability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive Curvature\n\n  * January 2003\n\nDOI:10.1090/conm/338/06080\n\nAuthors:\n\nKarl-Theodor Sturm\n\n  * University of Bonn\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research, you can request a copy directly from the author.\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe present an introduction to metric spaces of nonpositive curva- ture (\"NPC spaces\") and a discussion of barycenters of probability measures on such spaces. In our introduction to NPC spaces, we will concentrate on analytic and stochastic aspects of nonpositive curvature. Among others, we present two dierent characterizations of nonpositive curvature in terms of variance inequalities for probabilities on metric spaces as well as a character- ization in terms of a weighted quadruple inequality. The latter generalizes Reshetnyak's quadruple inequality which played a major role in many devel- opments during the last decade. For Riemannian manifolds, nonpositive cur- vature will also be characterized by the existence of a contracting barycenter map on the space of probability measures on the respective manifold. In our discussion of barycenters of probability measures on NPC spaces, basic results like the Law of Large Numbers, Jensen's inequality and the L1- contraction property will be derived and many examples will be presented. We identify barycenters for images, products, L2-spaces, Hilbert spaces, trees and manifolds. Also some results on convex means will be included.\n\n## No full-text available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the author.\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\n## Citations (429)\n\n## References (0)--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nContemporary Mathematics (https://www.iam.uni-bonn.de/fileadmin/WT/Inhalt/people/Karl-Theodor_Sturm/papers/paper41.pdf)\nciteturn3search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 23.3 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; # Probability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive CurvatureKarl-Theodor Sturm ... For Riemannian manifolds, nonpositive curvature will also be characterized by the existence of a contracting barycenter map on the space of probability measures on the respective manifold.\nContemporary Mathematics\n\n# Probability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive Curvature\n\nKarl-Theodor Sturm\n\n**Abstract.** We present an introduction to metric spaces of nonpositive curvature (“NPC spaces”) and a discussion of barycenters of probability measures on such spaces. In our introduction to NPC spaces, we will concentrate on analytic and stochastic aspects of nonpositive curvature. Among others, we present two different characterizations of nonpositive curvature in terms of variance inequalities for probabilities on metric spaces as well as a characterization in terms of a weighted quadruple inequality. The latter generalizes Reshetnyak’s quadruple inequality which played a major role in many developments during the last decade. For Riemannian manifolds, nonpositive curvature will also be characterized by the existence of a contracting barycenter map on the space of probability measures on the respective manifold.\n\nIn our discussion of barycenters of probability measures on NPC spaces, basic results like the Law of Large Numbers, Jensen’s inequality and the L^1-contraction property will be derived and many examples will be presented. We identify barycenters for images, products, L^2-spaces, Hilbert spaces, trees and manifolds. Also some results on convex means will be included.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. Geodesic Spaces  \n2. Global NPC Spaces  \n3. Examples of Global NPC Spaces  \n4. Barycenters  \n5. Identification of Barycenters  \n6. Jensen’s Inequality and L^1 Contraction Property  \n7. Convex Means  \n8. Local NPC Spaces  \nReferences\n\n1991 *Mathematics Subject Classification.* Primary 60B, 58E, 28C; Secondary 58C, 52A, 49C.  \n*Key words and phrases.* Barycenter, mean value, expectation, center of mass, nonpositive curvature, NPC space, Hadamard space, Alexandrov space, quadruple inequality, variance inequality, Jensen inequality.\n\nThe author gratefully acknowledges support by the SFB 611 at the University of Bonn.\n\n©0000 (copyright holder)\n\n1--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProbability measures on metric spaces of nonpositive curvature | CiNii Research (https://cir.nii.ac.jp/crid/1361418518709620864?lang=en)\nciteturn3search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Probability measures on metric spaces of nonpositive curvature ...   * Karl-Theodor Sturm ...     2003\n\n# Probability measures on metric spaces of nonpositive curvature\n\nDOI 14 Citations\n\n  * Karl-Theodor Sturm\n    \n    \n\n## Bibliographic Information\n\nPublished\n    2003\n\nDOI\n    \n\n  * 10.1090/conm/338/06080\n\nPublisher\n    American Mathematical Society\n\n## Search this article\n\n## Journal\n\n  * Contemporary Mathematics\n    \n\nContemporary Mathematics 357-390, 2003\n\nAmerican Mathematical Society\n\n## Citations (14)*help\n\nLoading...\n\nSee more\n\n## Details 詳細情報について\n\n  * CRID\n    1361418518709620864\n  * DOI\n    10.1090/conm/338/06080\n  * ISSN\n    10983627\n    02714132\n  * Data Source\n    \n    * Crossref--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4  KARL-THEODOR STURM (https://www.iam.uni-bonn.de/fileadmin/WT/Inhalt/people/Karl-Theodor_Sturm/papers/paper45.pdf)\nciteturn3search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 22.8 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; The property “nonnegative curvature” carries over from a metric space \\((N,d)\\) to the space of probability measures over this spaces [Ott01], [Stu01]. ... Probability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive Curvature ... Our definition of nonpositive curvature is completely analogous to our definition of nonnegative curvature in Definition 2.3.\n\n## 3. Probability Measures on Metric Spaces of Nonpositive Curvature\n\nThe next two sections are devoted to two generalizations of the class of Cartan-Hadamard manifolds. The first generalization is the class of metric spaces with nonpositive curvature with nonpositive curvature in the sense of Alexandrov. The second one (to be presented in the next section) will be the class of metric spaces which admit a contracting barycenter map. We summarize some of the basic results and refer to [Stu02] and [Stu03] for more details and further references.\n\n**Definition 3.1.** A metric space \\((N,d)\\) is called *global NPC space* if it is complete and if for all \\(k \\in \\mathbb{N}\\) and all \\(y_1,\\ldots,y_k \\in N\\)\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2k}\\sum_{i,j=1}^{k} d^2(y_i,y_j) \\ge \\inf_{z\\in N}\\frac{1}{k}\\sum_{i=1}^{k} d^2(z,y_i).\n\\]\n\nor, equivalently, if for all probability measures \\(q \\in \\mathcal{P}^2(N)\\)\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2}\\int_N \\int_N d^2(x,y)\\,q(dy)\\,q(dx) \\ge \\inf_{z\\in N}\\int_N d^2(z,x)\\,q(dx).\n\\]\n\nHere “NPC” stands for “nonpositive curvature” in the sense of A. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCAT(0) spaces on which a certain type of singularity is bounded (https://arxiv.org/abs/1010.1963)\nciteturn3academia17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 16.0 years ago; Authors: Tetsu Toyoda ... In this paper, we present a geometric condition for a family of CAT(0) spaces, which ensures that the Izeki-Nayatani invariants of spaces in the family are uniformly bounded from above by a constant strictly less than 1. ... Combining our result with a result of Izeki, Kondo and Nayatani, we see that random groups of Gromov's graph model have a fixed-point property for such a family.\nTitle: CAT(0) spaces on which a certain type of singularity is bounded\nAuthors: Tetsu Toyoda\nDate: Sun Oct 10 20:24:35 2010\n\nIn this paper, we present a geometric condition for a family of CAT(0) spaces, which ensures that the Izeki-Nayatani invariants of spaces in the family are uniformly bounded from above by a constant strictly less than 1. Each element of such a family with this condition is a space presented by M. Gromov as an example of a \"CAT(0) space with \"bounded\" singularities\". Combining our result with a result of Izeki, Kondo and Nayatani, we see that random groups of Gromov's graph model have a fixed-point property for such a family.-----------------------------------------------------